  "nl_text": "The database schema named \"schemabench_0078\" consists of three tables: \"pay_charges\", \"pay_subscriptions\", and \"(billable)\".\nThe \"pay_charges\" table is used to store information about payment charges. It includes columns such as \"id\", \"owner_type\", \"owner_id\", \"processor\", \"processor_id\", \"amount\", \"amount_refunded\", \"card_type\", \"card_last4\", \"card_exp_month\", \"card_exp_year\", \"created_at\", and \"updated_at\". The \"owner_id\" column is a foreign key referencing the \"id\" column in the \"(billable)\" table.\nThe \"pay_subscriptions\" table is used to store information about payment subscriptions. It includes columns such as \"id\", \"owner_id\", \"name\", \"processor\", \"processor_id\", \"processor_plan\", \"quantity\", \"trial_ends_at\", \"ends_at\", \"created_at\", \"updated_at\", and \"status\". The \"owner_id\" column is a foreign key referencing the \"id\" column in the \"(billable)\" table.\nThe \"(billable)\" table is used to store information about billable entities. It includes columns such as \"id\", \"processor\", \"processor_id\", \"trial_ends_at\", \"card_type\", \"card_last4\", \"card_exp_month\", \"card_exp_year\", and \"extra_billing_info\". It does not have any foreign key references.\nThis schema is designed with the aim of managing and tracking various aspects of payment transactions, including charges and subscriptions, and billable entities. It ensures data integrity by enforcing constraints on the tables, and referential integrity by maintaining relationships between the tables.",
  "gold_question": "Background / Context\n\nThe project involves developing a payments engine specifically designed for Ruby on Rails (version 6.0 and higher), aimed at managing payments and subscriptions. It integrates with several payment processors including Stripe, Paddle, Braintree, and Lemon Squeezy, with additional support for a fake processor for testing purposes.\n\nObjectives\n\nThe primary objective is to facilitate secure and efficient handling of payment transactions and managing subscriptions across multiple processors. The system must support Strong Customer Authentication (SCA) and accommodate payments via credit card and PayPal where applicable.\n\nStakeholders & Users\n\n- End Users: Individuals or businesses using the Ruby on Rails application who require subscription management and payment processing.\n- Developers: Ruby on Rails developers integrating the payment engine into their applications.\n- Administrators: Personnel responsible for overseeing payment processing and managing subscriptions.\n\nFunctional Descriptions\n\n1. Payment Processing:\n   - Integrate with supported processors: Stripe, Paddle, Braintree, Lemon Squeezy, and a fake processor for testing.\n   - Handle payment transactions securely using current SCA protocols.\n   - Support PayPal payments where applicable.\n\n2. Subscription Management:\n   - Create, update, and terminate subscriptions.\n   - Track subscription details, including plan type, quantity, and status.\n   - Manage trial periods and subscription end dates.\n\n3. Transaction Tracking:\n   - Record detailed information about each transaction, including amount, refund status, and payment method details.\n   - Store and update transactional data securely.\n\nNon-Functional Descriptions\n\n- The system must be compatible with Ruby on Rails 6.0 and higher.\n- Ensure data security and integrity in line with the latest SCA requirements.\n- Provide a testing environment using a fake processor to facilitate application development and testing without real financial transactions.",
  "input_json": "/data/SchemaBench/Experiment/schema2text_deepseek/0078.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0078\nCREATE TABLE `billable` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `processor` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `processor_id` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `trial_ends_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `card_type` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `card_last4` char(4) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `card_exp_month` int(2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `card_exp_year` int(4) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `extra_billing_info` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `pay_charges` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `owner_type` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `owner_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `processor` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `processor_id` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `amount` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `amount_refunded` decimal(10,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `card_type` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `card_last4` char(4) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `card_exp_month` int(2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `card_exp_year` int(4) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `pay_charges_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`owner_id`) REFERENCES `billable` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `pay_subscriptions` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `owner_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `processor` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `processor_id` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `processor_plan` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `quantity` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `trial_ends_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `ends_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `pay_subscriptions_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`owner_id`) REFERENCES `billable` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
